// What things are worth, in gold (engine/src/value.rs; the design wiki's P51 price curve,
// draft 52): `base` coins at level 1, `growth` times as much every `per` levels, rounded to
// the nearest `step` above `round_above`, times the rarity's factor. A thing's level is what
// it takes to use it: the Defence that wears it, the level that wields it, or the lowest
// level of a recipe that makes it; a made thing is worth at least `crafted` times what goes
// into one of it, by its cheapest recipe, raw materials counting `raw` each. Death keeps the `kept` units worth most (`warded` with a
// grave-ward amulet, kept besides), counted one at a time, so a stack or a purse keeps one;
// the rest lies `grave` seconds where they fell, theirs alone (`warded_grave` warded). A
// prayer that keeps more (Keepsake) never takes it past `most`, so it doesn't stack with the
// amulet (design d86).
(
    base: 2.0,
    growth: 2.5,
    per: 15.0,
    round_above: 100,
    step: 5,
    rarity: (common: 1, uncommon: 2, rare: 5, very_rare: 12, legendary: 30),
    crafted: 1.25,
    // A raw material (nothing makes, wears or wields it) counts this many coins times its
    // rarity's factor inside a made thing (P51, draft 73); its own price is the curve's.
    raw: 0.5,
    // Worth a set number of coins whatever their level. A cured hide took ten minutes on a
    // rack, so it is worth more than the raw one off the beast (the curve's 2).
    fixed: {"base:gold_coin": 1, "base:hide": 3},
    // Priced on the curve at a set level, where nothing wears, wields or makes them at one:
    // Old Tusk's charm at his level (creatures_bosses.ron), so death keeps it before
    // everyday gear.
    levels: {"base:charge_charm": 10},
    death: (kept: 3, warded: 4, most: 4, grave: 1800.0, warded_grave: 3600.0),
)
